    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The discovery of hydrocarbon reservoirs in fractured granitic rocks has focused the attention of some oil and gas companies on problems that they previously have ignored: (1)what are common distributions and geometries of fractures in granitic rocks;(2) how does faulting in granitic rock effect the local porosity and permeability; and(3) what are the implications for the spatial variations of fracture permeability in granitic rocks? These questions are addressed by reviewing a case study of the development of faults and related fractures in the granitic rocks of the MountAbbot quadrangle in the central Sierra Nevada of California.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
